Objective

Create a reusable playbook that:

* Creates an administrative user.
* Assigns a password securely.
* Adds the user to the sudo group.
* Creates the home directory.
* Installs an SSH public key.
* Uses Ansible Vault so passwords are never stored in plaintext.

Create the Vault File
mkdir -p inventory/group_vars/all
touch inventory/group_vars/all/vault.yml

Encrypt it:
ansible-vault encrypt inventory/group_vars/all/vault.yml

Edit the Vault
ansible-vault edit inventory/group_vars/all/vault.yml

Generate a Linux Password Hash
openssl passwd -6

Store the Hash in Vault
* you do this with ansible edit

users.yml
---
- name: Configure administrative users
  hosts: droplet
  become: true

  tasks:

    - name: Ensure sudo is installed
      ansible.builtin.apt:
        name: sudo
        state: present
        update_cache: true

    - name: Create adminja account
      ansible.builtin.user:
        name: adminja
        password: "{{ vault_adminja_password_hash }}"
        groups:
          - sudo
        append: true
        shell: /bin/bash
        create_home: true
        state: present
        update_password: on_create

    - name: Install SSH public key
      ansible.posix.authorized_key:
        user: adminja
        state: present
        key: "{{ lookup('file', lookup('env', 'HOME') + '/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub') }}"
		
		
Run the Playbook
ansible-playbook \
-i inventory/infrastructure.ini \
playbooks/users.yml \
--ask-vault-pass